<title>UK: Italy sets one billion euro seven-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>Italy sets one billion euro seven-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Paribas and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ITALY</p>
<p> AMT    1.0 BLN EURO  COUPON     **	  MATURITY    02.APR.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    02.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.30	REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+18 BP</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE PRICED LATER.</p>
<p>		PAYMENTS IN ECU UNTIL EMU.</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA	  DENOMS (K) 1	   SALE LIMITS US/GB</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ITALY     HOME CTRY  ITALY     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.10	SELL CONC  0.20	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.00 PCT OAT DUE 2004</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
